  "tier": "sonnet",
  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: fix round 1 for T-1406: restore rerun candidate extraction so argument-like ids stay audited as rejected",
  "spec": "Why: T-1406's gate went red on tests/test_daemon.py test_rerun_rejects_argument_like_ids: resume_hint.rejected_ids lost '--rootdir=/'. Besides the requested quota change, T-1406 changed failures._test_id_candidates to keep only _TEST_ID_TOKEN matches from a FAILED line, so argument-like tokens are no longer candidates and are no longer recorded as rejected. That audit is a safety property (argument injection into the rerun command); the spec never asked to change candidate extraction.\n\nWhat (in wt/T-1406 on task/T-1406, on top of its commit): restore _test_id_candidates to the original split (line[7:].split(\" - \", 1)[0].split()) so every token is a candidate and invalid ones land in rejected_ids as before. Keep everything else from T-1406: _TEST_ID_TOKEN used only by _strip_test_ids, _QUOTA_MARKER with word boundaries, the gate_red skip of the quota branch, and tests/test_failures.py::test_gate_red_with_cooling_test_id_is_not_quota.\n\nCommit, then run tests/test_failures.py and tests/test_daemon.py -k \"rerun or quota or failure_kind\" in the foreground. Never background a command, never the full gate.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1418"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_rerun_rejects_argument_like_ids passes: rejected_ids is {'--rootdir=/', '../x.py::t'} again",
    "tests/test_failures.py::test_gate_red_with_cooling_test_id_is_not_quota still passes",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/T-1406 exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/failures.py",
    "tests/test_failures.py"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
  "constraints": {
    "read_only": true,
    "budget_turns": 20,
    "timeout_s": 900
  },
  "status": "done",
  "assigned_to": "claude:A",
  "worktree": "/Users/k3ntaw/code/orchestrator/wt/T-1424",
  "codex_thread": null,
  "result": {
    "summary": "Both listed acceptance tests pass and the gate_red short-circuit logic is correctly preserved, but _test_id_candidates was not restored to the literal original split as the spec explicitly instructed \u2014 it gained a new, unrequested removesuffix rule for '(missing: test not defined)' lines, bundled with an unlisted test change. Functionally low risk (rejected_ids is audit-only, not fed into the rerun command), but it deviates from spec and expands scope in a security-flagged code path without authorization.",
    "verdict": "request_changes",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/failures.py",
        "line": 40,
        "issue": "Spec says to restore _test_id_candidates to the literal original expression `line[7:].split(\" - \", 1)[0].split()` (verified this is exactly the pre-T-1406 code at commit b5c26d0). The diff instead adds an unrequested `.removesuffix(\" (missing: test not defined)\")` call before the split, which is new logic never present in the original and not asked for by the spec. It changes real runtime behavior for gate_red 'missing test not defined' FAILED lines (which predate T-1406, e.g. test_gate_red_when_acceptance_test_missing) so they no longer populate rejected_ids with the extra split tokens the original 'restore to original, as before' behavior would have produced. The diff also bakes this unrequested behavior into an existing shared test (test_test_ids_reject_shell_and_traversal) that isn't listed in the packet's 'changed tests' section. This is scope creep beyond the explicit restore instruction, in a function the packet calls out as a safety/audit property (argument-injection rejection audit) \u2014 it should not be modified beyond what was asked without going back through spec review.",
        "severity": "med"
      }
    ],
