    {
      "ts": 1790809196.421142,
      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "Both listed acceptance tests pass and the gate_red short-circuit logic is correctly preserved, but _test_id_candidates was not restored to the literal original split as the spec explicitly instructed \u2014 it gained a new, unrequested removesuffix rule for '(missing: test not defined)' lines, bundled with an unlisted test change. Functionally low risk (rejected_ids is audit-only, not fed into the rerun command), but it deviates from spec and expands scope in a security-flagged code path without authorization.",
        "verdict": "request_changes",
        "comments": [
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/failures.py",
            "line": 40,
            "issue": "Spec says to restore _test_id_candidates to the literal original expression `line[7:].split(\" - \", 1)[0].split()` (verified this is exactly the pre-T-1406 code at commit b5c26d0). The diff instead adds an unrequested `.removesuffix(\" (missing: test not defined)\")` call before the split, which is new logic never present in the original and not asked for by the spec. It changes real runtime behavior for gate_red 'missing test not defined' FAILED lines (which predate T-1406, e.g. test_gate_red_when_acceptance_test_missing) so they no longer populate rejected_ids with the extra split tokens the original 'restore to original, as before' behavior would have produced. The diff also bakes this unrequested behavior into an existing shared test (test_test_ids_reject_shell_and_traversal) that isn't listed in the packet's 'changed tests' section. This is scope creep beyond the explicit restore instruction, in a function the packet calls out as a safety/audit property (argument-injection rejection audit) \u2014 it should not be modified beyond what was asked without going back through spec review.",
            "severity": "med"
          }
        ],
        "packet_version": "c1dbd663e0df",
        "confidence": 0.0,
        "provenance": [
          "repo"
        ]
      }
